Objectives 

1. To represent a sensor network using a weighted undirected graph.
2. To implement Prim’s algorithm to find a minimum spanning tree.
3. To display each selected communication link with its weight and running total cost.
4. To allow the user to update the weight of an existing edge and run Prim’s algorithm again.
5. To detect disconnected graphs and determine whether a spanning tree can be formed.
6. To understand the practical application of minimum spanning trees in sensor networks.
